This project implements clean-room Rust and Solidity verification components
and test vectors (crates/, contracts/) interoperating with the following
Apache-2.0 open-source projects. The SP1 segment guest (sp1/) instead builds
SASH's own source, modified as described below.

1. SASH zk-inference-prover (https://github.com/sg-ai-safety-hub/zk-inference-prover)
   Pinned reference revision: eb95bfa887299d1637550228d42086c27cbb2b3b
   License: Apache-2.0

2. Stwo / NitrooZK-stwo (https://github.com/starkware-libs/stwo and
   https://github.com/AntChainOpenLabs/NitrooZK-stwo)
   Pinned reference revision: 41c2a05bdb1fc3e3762bc7804108e8bc269bb6fc
   License: Apache-2.0

3. TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0 (https://huggingface.co/TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0)
   Pinned reference revision: fe8a4ea1ffedaf415f4da2f062534de366a451e6
   License: Apache-2.0

Modified upstream source (Apache-2.0 §4(b)). sp1/scripts/vendor-sash.sh
downloads SASH zk-inference-prover at eb95bfa887299d1637550228d42086c27cbb2b3b,
which vendors NitrooZK-stwo under nitroo/, and applies the patches in
sp1/patches/ (all of them for sp1/vendor/sash, patch 0006 alone for
sp1/vendor/sash-oracle). Each patch's header states what it changes and why.
The files the patches modify:

